<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammadu Korau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammadu Korau is remembered in tradition as the first Muslim king of Katsina, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> kingdoms of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, and is usually dated to the second half of the 15th century. Tradition also makes Korau a wrestler who killed Sanau, last ruler of the earlier Durbawa line, and founded a new dynasty, though the early chronology is uncertain. The Gobarau mosque is associated with his reign.</p></div>
